spect of child sexual  abuse and indeed others they may wish to  include an absolute priority the  Catholic and Anglican churches have  apologized for their failings but the  proposed conditions for mandatory  reporting are limited to things such as  someone actually confessing to abuse or  being abused it's uh proposing criminal  offenses in relation to a very narrow  set of situations but the vast majority  of the situations that the inquiry  actually saw in evidence where there was  a failure to report would not be subject  to that criminal penalty and that's our  concern survivors like Joanne relived  their past to safeguard Children of the  future it's up to the government now to  ensure that that courage is rewarded  Jason Farrell Sky News
 

